<article class="env-lemma" id="074C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/074C">Lemma <span data-tag="074C">11.4.4</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a $k$-algebra. Let $K$ be a central $k$-algebra which is a skew field. Then any two-sided ideal $I \subset A \otimes _ k K$ is of the form $J \otimes _ k K$ for some two-sided ideal $J \subset A$. In particular, if $A$ is simple, then so is $A \otimes _ k K$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Set $J = \{ a \in A \mid a \otimes 1 \in I\} $. This is a two-sided ideal of $A$. And $I = J \otimes _ k K$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/074B" data-tag="074B">11.4.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>